project KSHIAI_BATTLE_PERCEPTION:
  version 2
  title "Observer-relative battle perception and qualitative self feedback"
  description |
    Extend the accepted semantic world with explicit self anchoring,
    deterministic qualitative effect and strain cues, multi-modal perception,
    and anonymous observer-local contacts without exposing hidden mechanics or
    canonical source identity.
  as_of 2026-08-04
  duration_unit day
  finish PERCEPTION_ACCEPTED

resource DEV:
  title "Developer"
  capacity 1

milestone CURRENT_BEHAVIOR:
  title "Existing semantic observation and cognition behavior assessed"
  state reached

milestone DESIGN_READY:
  title "Observer-relative perception decisions and boundaries ready"
  state reached

milestone SCHEMA_READY:
  title "Perception frame and private contact-ledger schemas ready"
  state reached

milestone PROMPT_STRATEGY_READY:
  title "Combined or split perception prompt topology selected from evidence"

milestone EVIDENCE_READY:
  title "Mechanical and semantic perception evidence contracts ready"

milestone QUALITATIVE_CUES_READY:
  title "Deterministic effect and strain cues ready"

milestone PROJECTION_READY:
  title "Side-specific multi-modal projection and anonymous contacts ready"

milestone NARRATION_VIEWS_READY:
  title "Perspective-specific narration views and ID containment ready"

milestone CONSUMERS_READY:
  title "Character agents and narration consume bounded perception frames"

milestone COMPATIBILITY_READY:
  title "Compatibility privacy failure and bounded-state behavior verified"

milestone PERCEPTION_ACCEPTED:
  title "Observer-relative battle perception accepted"

task T_DESIGN CURRENT_BEHAVIOR -> DESIGN_READY:
  title "Specify qualitative self cognition and observer-relative perception"
  description |
    Record llmthink decisions that preserve canonical world truth while
    separating explicit self perception, identified entities, unknown contacts,
    ambient phenomena, and private interpretation. Define the no-extra-call
    preferred pipeline, accuracy-gated split topology, absolute and relative
    bands, required counterpart slots, contact lifecycle, narration views,
    non-leakage, and provider-failure boundaries before implementation.
  duration 1d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_SCHEMA DESIGN_READY -> SCHEMA_READY:
  title "Define perception frames cues references and bounded private ledgers"
  description |
    Add shared schemas for observer and self references, sensory modalities,
    phenomena, direction, distance, salience, occurrence and attribution
    certainty, identified subjects, anonymous observer-local contacts,
    qualitative absolute and relative effect and reserve cues, required self and
    counterpart slots, and bounded current contact continuity. Define separate
    character-frame and ephemeral narration-view schemas. Keep unknown canonical
    source mappings out of character-facing DTOs. Add schema and boundary tests.
  duration 2d
  status done
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROMPT_STRATEGY SCHEMA_READY -> PROMPT_STRATEGY_READY:
  title "Evaluate combined versus separated world and sensory prompts"
  description |
    Build fixed provider and model fixtures for one combined reconciler response
    and for separate world-patch and sensory-evidence prompts. Measure schema-valid
    rate, patch correctness, sensory coverage, attribution and identity errors,
    latency, and token cost. Record the accepted topology per provider and model;
    do not introduce per-turn adaptive repair calls.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_EVIDENCE PROMPT_STRATEGY_READY -> EVIDENCE_READY:
  title "Produce validated mechanical and semantic perception evidence"
  description |
    Derive authoritative mechanical evidence after resolution and extend the
    selected prompt topology with a separately validated sensory-evidence
    section or call. Ground every source and target in committed action, event,
    and semantic references; reject invalid evidence independently from a valid
    world patch. Add provider, validation, and failure tests without prose-pattern
    mechanics.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_QUALITATIVE_CUES EVIDENCE_READY -> QUALITATIVE_CUES_READY:
  title "Derive deterministic hand-feel impact and exertion bands"
  description |
    Calculate delivered and received post-mitigation changes on independent
    absolute and target-relative axes plus current vitality stamina and focus
    reserve bands. Cover loss gain no-effect immunity incapacity overkill
    simultaneous multi-target and environment outcomes. Keep thresholds and raw
    ratios server-only and add monotonic boundary and A/B metamorphic tests.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_PROJECT QUALITATIVE_CUES_READY -> PROJECTION_READY:
  title "Project perceived events modalities and contacts per observer"
  description |
    In one deterministic stage combine committed event evidence qualitative cues
    and validated sensory evidence into frozen A and B frames. Always emit self
    and counterpart slots with independent current access and identity knowledge.
    Support multi-modal identified contact and ambient subjects update bounded
    server-private registries issue non-reused IDs split ambiguous groups only
    prospectively and redact unknown canonical identity and exact hidden location.
    Add projection lifecycle capacity and side-swap tests.
  duration 3d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_NARRATION_VIEWS PROJECTION_READY -> NARRATION_VIEWS_READY:
  title "Build narration views and contain identifiers by perspective"
  description |
    Derive first-person opponent-limited omniscient external and fluid-focus views
    without another LLM call. Mark the viewpoint subject explicitly include all
    IDs only for omniscient input omit IDs for external input and attach safe
    render labels to every reference. Add strong narrator prompt constraints and
    deterministic exact ID-to-label replacement for paragraphs and speeches.
    Test the complete perspective matrix and leakage repair.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_CONSUMERS NARRATION_VIEWS_READY -> CONSUMERS_READY:
  title "Integrate frozen perception frames with agents and narration"
  description |
    Give each character only its explicit self-labelled frame, previous private
    continuity, and validated available actions; counterpart name and condition
    are present only when identified. Update provider contracts prompts mocks and
    fallbacks for the selected combined or split topology. Feed the existing
    narrator call only its derived view and preserve uncertainty without granting
    any consumer mutation authority. Add service-level wiring tests for A and B.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_COMPAT CONSUMERS_READY -> COMPATIBILITY_READY:
  title "Verify legacy fallback privacy failure and size behavior"
  description |
    Seed active legacy counterparts as identified from setup, preserve previous
    agent state and registry on provider or projection failure, emit a minimal
    engine-authored self frame, bound contact and perception retention, prevent
    unknown identity through snapshots diffs logs prompts DTOs and tooling, and
    verify that ledgers freeze serially before parallel A and B advancement.
  duration 2d
  requires:
    DEV 1

task T_ACCEPT COMPATIBILITY_READY -> PERCEPTION_ACCEPTED:
  title "Accept self feedback anonymous perception and non-leakage scenarios"
  description |
    Accept combined or split prompt evidence, absolute and relative hit and
    fatigue feedback, required not-perceived and unidentified counterpart slots,
    source-less footsteps, partial multi-modal identification, contact split and
    eviction, prospective reveal, ambiguous effects, every narration perspective,
    provider and projection failure, and absence of hidden totals, hidden identity,
    exact hidden positions, unconditional foe knowledge, and user-visible IDs.
    Run llmthink and PERT audits plus test typecheck and build.
  duration 1d
  requires:
    DEV 1
